            "type": "concept",
            "title": "Relative vs Absolute",
            "body": "Relative risk compares two groups: 'a 25% reduction'. Absolute risk names the size of the thing being changed: 'from 4 in 100 to 3 in 100'. Both describe the same study honestly. Relative figures are always the larger-sounding pair, so they are the ones that get printed.",
