            "type": "example",
            "title": "Where the Exaggeration Starts",
            "body": "In 2014, Petroc Sumner and colleagues traced 462 UK university press releases into the news that followed (BMJ). A third turned a correlation into a cause. Where the release exaggerated, 81% of the resulting stories did too; where it did not, 18% did. The overstatement usually began before the journalist.",
            "art": "seed"
