            "body": "Wet surfaces cannot get hot. Boiling water pins the surface near 100 degrees, well below Maillard territory, and a crowded pan traps the escaping steam. Patting meat dry and leaving space between pieces is not fussiness; it is the difference between a brown crust and grey stewing.",
