            "body": "Aryabhata says the sky does not turn; you do. Just as a man in a boat moving downstream sees the trees on the bank slide backwards, he writes, so a person on the equator sees the stars move west. He also explains eclipses as shadows, the Earth's and the Moon's, rather than as a demon swallowing the Sun.",
            "art": "orbit"
