              "Partial reprogramming rewinds epigenetic age, but leaving the factors on produces fatal teratomas — which is why protocols are pulsed and why cancer risk is the field's central obstacle.",
              "Ocampo 2016 extended lifespan in progeroid mice and improved tissue repair in normal ones; it did not show lifespan extension in normal mice.",
              "Plasma dilution reproduced much of young blood's benefit, suggesting removal of old factors may matter more than addition of young ones.",
              "For any new claim, ask: species, endpoint, age at start, sex, replication, and who paid."
