            "body": "A newborn a few days old prefers her mother's voice to a stranger's. Anthony DeCasper and William Fifer showed in 1980 that babies will change how they suck on a dummy just to hear it. She also prefers face-shaped patterns, and the rhythm of the language she heard through the womb wall.",
