            "body": "A child meets the world with schemas. New things get pulled into an existing one — every four-legged animal is a doggie — until the mismatch grows too great and the schema splits to accommodate a horse. Development, for Piaget, is this pair grinding against each other, not information piling up.",
            "art": "puzzle"
