            "type": "concept",
            "title": "What Survived, What Did Not",
            "body": "The sharp ages and hard stage boundaries did not hold: competence turns up earlier on easier tasks and later on harder ones, and children slide between levels depending on the material. Whether stages are real or a useful summary is still argued. What survived is that children build understanding by acting.",
