            "type": "concept",
            "title": "The Two Kinds of Wanting",
            "art": "flame",
            "body": "Williams splits desires in two. Conditional desires assume you will be around anyway: if I am alive on Tuesday, I want this tooth fixed. Categorical desires work the other way, giving you a reason to be around at all: finish the book, raise the child, see how the trial ends. Only the second kind answers the question of whether to go on."
