            "title": "The Flying Buttress",
            "body": "Gothic builders wanted tall thin walls full of glass, but their stone vaults still shoved outward. The flying buttress is the honest answer: an arm of masonry standing outside the building that catches the thrust and walks it down to a heavy pier. The structure is not concealed. It is put on show and made beautiful.",
