            "body": "Robert Moses reshaped New York for forty years without ever winning an election. Jane Jacobs was a magazine writer on Hudson Street who believed he was destroying the thing he claimed to be improving. Their collision in the early 1960s is the argument every city is still having, and each of them was partly right.",
