            "title": "Lines That Slide",
            "body": "Move a source toward you and every line shifts to shorter wavelengths; move it away and they all shift longer, by the same fraction. Measure the shift and you have a speed, which is how astronomers weigh binary stars and detect planets. For very distant galaxies a second cause takes over: the space in between stretches while the light is in flight.",
