            "type": "example",
            "title": "Counting the Imprisoned",
            "body": "Imprisonment rates per 100,000 people vary far more between countries than crime rates do. The United States holds roughly 530; England and Wales about 140; Germany around 70; Japan under 40. Since a state of exception began in 2022, El Salvador has passed 1,000, the highest rate recorded anywhere. These are policy choices, not natural facts.",
            "art": "graph"
