            "type": "concept",
            "title": "Restorative Justice",
            "body": "A different question: not what does he deserve, but what does repair require? Aotearoa New Zealand has made this the default for young offenders since 1989, when the Children, Young Persons, and Their Families Act put the family group conference, drawing on Māori practice, at the centre of youth justice. Victim, offender, families and community meet and agree what happens next.",
            "art": "dialog"
