            "type": "concept",
            "title": "The Personal Question",
            "body": "The personal version asks about a life from the inside: do your days add up to anything? Most philosophers now work on this one, and mark it with a preposition — meaning in life rather than the meaning of life. Thaddeus Metz makes the split explicit in Meaning in Life (2013).",
            "art": "path"
