            "type": "example",
            "title": "Tolstoy Hides the Rope",
            "body": "By his fifties Leo Tolstoy had written War and Peace and Anna Karenina, and had land, family, health and fame. Then one question stopped him: what will come of what I do today? In A Confession he writes that he hid a cord from himself so he would not hang himself, and stopped hunting with a gun.",
